// Spoken lines for the villagers, kept apart from the profiles so npc_data.js stays
// a readable character sheet. npc_data.js merges these into NPC_PROFILES:
//   FACT_SAY[factId]        the fact as the villager says it (facts are written for Lyra's
//                           notes, in the third person; dialogue needs their own voice)
//   NPC_EXTRA_LINES[npcId]  round-2 lines:
//     cold        greetings for a day after the player hurt someone in the village
//     crime       shouts while the player is wanted (fleeing, calling the guard)
//     shaken      after being knocked out, for the rest of that day
//     wronged     to the player who knocked them out or struck them
//     refuse      a shop turning the player away
//     lyraAlone   to Lyra when she is living apart from the player
//     aboutLyra   to the player about Lyra: { apart, left, gone }
//     askPrompt   before a question; noMore when they have nothing new; notYet when
//                 they know more but do not trust the player enough to say it
//     helped      when the player helps them up after a knock-out (someone else's doing)

